{{Quote|Metal - meet magnetism!|Lodestar, before using his powers on [[Rex Salazar (Generator Rex)|Rex]].<ref name="HU">''[[Ben 10-Generator Rex: Heroes United|Ben 10/Generator Rex: Heroes United]]''</ref>}}
Lodestar is magnetokinetic, meaning that he is able to control the natural magnetic fields around him,{{Refn|''[[Ben 10 Ultimate Alien: The Complete Guide]]'', [[:File:Elecronian from Electront.png|Page 36]]|group = guide|name = guide}} and also generate and project his own fields; which are capable of overloading electrical circuits, attracting magnetic materials and ferromagnetic metals to himself. At full power, his magnetic pulse can affect machinery as far as half a mile.{{Refn|[[:File:Lodestar Alien Creation Card.png]]|group = Bandai|name = card}} Lodestar's powers even work on mechanical beings like [[Ultimate Sonorosian]]s<ref>''[[Absolute Power: Part 2]]''</ref> and [[Chronosapien]]s.{{Refn|[[:File:Chronosapiens Can Be Magnetized.PNG]]|group = DJW}} Lodestar is also capable of using electromagnetism, as shown when Lodestar generated an electromagnetic force field around himself.<ref name="UA">''[[Ultimate Aggregor (Episode)|Ultimate Aggregor]]''</ref>

Lodestar can use his magnetic fields to block solar energy attacks.<ref name="Vendetta" />

Lodestar has telekinetic control over metal, allowing him to levitate and move it around without physical contact.<ref name="BB" /> He can also use this "magno-telekinesis" to make himself levitate<ref>''[[Absolute Power: Part 1]]''</ref> and fly for short distances.{{Refn|group = Bandai|name = card}}<ref name="UA"/>

Lodestar can use his magnetism to damage and destroy any magnetic substance at will, as seen when he opened the [[Naljian Destructor]] and attempted to destroy it afterwards,<ref name="BB">''[[Busy Box]]''</ref> dismantled a [[Techadon Robot]],<ref>''[[Primus (Episode)|Primus]]''</ref> and tore apart the [[Toltech Battle Armor]].<ref name="Duped" /> He can also do this by converting his magnetic fields into kinetic energy, as shown when he made one of [[Computron's Minions|Computron's minions]] explode from afar.<ref>''[[Girl Trouble]]''</ref>

Lodestar is able to render other materials magnetic, such as when he caused the Toltech Battle Armor to attract benches, trash cans and even [[Kevin's Car (Original)|Kevin's car]] towards itself.<ref name="Duped" />

If Lodestar gets destroyed by something, such as [[Aggregor]]'s [[Aggregor's Starship|starship]] self-detonating, he can reconstitute by pulling his shattered pieces back together with his magnetism.<ref name="UA" />

Lodestar possesses enhanced strength, as he was able to briefly grapple with the [[Stalker]] but with some difficulty.<ref name="VG" /> Furthermore, if an ally like [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]] absorbs metal, Lodestar can use his magnetism to throw said ally toward their enemies.<ref>''[[The Purge]]''</ref><ref>''[[The More Things Change: Part 1]]''</ref>

Lodestar possesses enhanced durability, as he was able to withstand being hurt by the red troops' laser blasts,<ref name="Simple">''[[Simple]]''</ref> being thrown through the walls of a house,<ref name="VG">''[[Video Games (Episode)|Video Games]]''</ref> and the [[Red Knight]]'s throwing stars.<ref name="RtF">''[[Return to Forever]]''</ref>

Lodestar can survive in the vacuum of space.{{Refn|[[:File:Lodestar Space Survivability.PNG]]|group = DJW}}

Using the electromagnetic spectrum, Lodestar can see objects like on a radar screen.{{Refn|group = Bandai|name = card}}

Lodestar can act as a compass.{{Refn|[[:File:Lodestar Compass.PNG]]|group = DJW}}

==Weaknesses==
<gallery type="slideshow">
RtF (206).png|Ineffective Magnetism
RtF (225).png|Vulnerable Head
NotLN (191).png|Magnetism Vulnerability
</gallery>
{{Quote|Magnets, huh? Well, there's no metal in pavement!|Rex countering Lodestar's magnetism.<ref name="HU" />}}
Lodestar's magnetic fields are useless against non-magnetic objects, such as road pavement,<ref name="HU" /> the [[Red Knight]]'s throwing knives,<ref name="RtF" /> and the Stalker.<ref name="VG" /> Additionally, Lodestar's magnetic fields can also be absorbed and redirected by certain substances, such as the [[Shock Staff]].<ref name="NotLN">''[[Night of the Living Nightmare]]''</ref>

Lodestar's head is a very vulnerable target for his opponents due to it not being attached to his body. Lodestar's opponents can take advantage of this weakness in various ways, such as grabbing it, which will forcefully pull Lodestar's body alongside his head,<ref name="VG" /> throwing objects at it, such as the [[Red Knight]]'s throwing stars, which will cause his head to start spinning<ref name="RtF" /> or knocking it away with a magnetic field.<ref name="NotLN" />

==History==
===Alien Force===
*In ''[[War of the Worlds: Part 2]]'', Lodestar was unlocked onscreen after the [[Omnitrix (Original)|Omnitrix]] was reset and [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] immediately transformed into him off-screen.
*Lodestar first appeared in ''[[Simple]]'', where he defeated the red troops and tried to reason with them.
*In ''[[Busy Box]]'', Lodestar battled the [[Naljian Destructor]] and ripped it open to release its cube form but was unable to destroy it when [[Cosmic Mom]] arrived.
*In ''[[Primus (Episode)|Primus]]'', Lodestar fought and dismantled a red [[Techadon Robot]] but reverted before he could destroy it.
*In ''[[Vendetta]]'', Lodestar battled [[Ragnarok]] until the latter escaped.
*In ''[[The Final Battle: Part 2]]'', Lodestar was briefly used by [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]]'s [[Bioid]]s.

===Ultimate Alien===
*In ''[[Duped]]'', Lodestar defeated [[Sir Urien]].
*In ''[[Video Games (Episode)|Video Games]]'', Lodestar was defeated by the [[Stalker]].
*In ''[[Ultimate Aggregor (Episode)|Ultimate Aggregor]]'', Lodestar and [[Alien Force|the team]] defeated a group of [[Aggrebot]]s. Afterwards, Lodestar boarded [[Aggregor]]'s [[Aggregor's Starship|starship]] and was destroyed when it exploded but survived and regenerated.
*In ''[[Absolute Power: Part 1]]'', Lodestar violently attacked some [[Forever Knights]] to find out about [[Ultimate Kevin]]'s location.
*In ''[[Girl Trouble]]'', Lodestar battled some of [[Computron]]'s [[Computron's Minions|minions]].
*In ''[[The Purge]]'', Lodestar fought a [[Mech Dragon|mechanical dragon]] and destroyed it with [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]]'s help.
*In ''[[Ben 10-Generator Rex: Heroes United|Ben 10/Generator Rex: Heroes United]]'', Lodestar battled [[Rex Salazar (Generator Rex)|Rex]] before switching into [[Rath (Classic)|Rath]].
*In ''[[Night of the Living Nightmare]]'', Lodestar appeared twice in a dream. Firstly, Ben as Lodestar, without a head, defeated Aggregor. Later, Lodestar was seen confronting [[Albedo]].

===Omniverse===
*In ''[[The More Things Change: Part 1]]'', Lodestar stopped [[Zombozo (Classic)|Zombozo]] from stealing a brain from the brain bank.
*In ''[[Return to Forever]]'', Lodestar battled the [[Forever Knights]] and saved [[Jimmy Jones|Jimmy]] from them.
*In ''[[A New Dawn]]'', Lodestar appeared for a short time when [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] was cycling through his aliens.

