==Etymology==
A lodestar is a star used as a navigation reference, particularly a pole star, such as [[Wikipedia:Polaris|Polaris]].

It is also etymologically connected to [[Wikipedia:Lodestone|lodestone]], a naturally magnetized piece of the mineral called [[Wikipedia:Magnetite|magnetite]].{{Refn|[[:File:Lodestar Etymology.PNG]]|group = DM}}

==Trivia==
*Lodestar's hologram in ''[[War of the Worlds: Part 2]]'' uses his concept design as a base.{{Refn|[[:File:Lodestar AF Concept.png]]|group = ca}}
*Lodestar is the first alien used on-screen by 16-year-old Ben in [https://ben10.fandom.com/wiki/Ben_10:_Omniverse_(TV_Series) Omniverse]. 
*In '''[[Ben 10: Alien Force (TV Series)|Alien Force]]''' and '''[[Ben 10: Ultimate Alien (TV Series)|Ultimate Alien]]''', Lodestar appeared to have a mouth, but with the exception of several errors, it never opened. However, in '''Omniverse''', his mouth moves when he talks, much like [[Eatle]].
*Lodestar's magnetic pulses have changed color throughout his appearances:
**In ''[[Simple]]'', the pulses were white.
**In his subsequent '''Alien Force''' appearances, they were green.
**In '''Ultimate Alien''', they were white again.
**In ''[[Ben 10-Generator Rex: Heroes United|Heroes United]]'' and '''Omniverse''', they are green again.
*In the code Nano section on the ''[[FusionFall]]'' website, a picture of Lodestar's head can be seen.
*The '''[[Ben 10 (2016 TV Series)|Ben 10]]''' reboot game ''Brains vs. Bugs'' has a magnet upgrade that resembles Lodestar's upper body minus the shoulders, arms, and head.
*Lodestar's skin pattern can change like flowing ink with shifts in the magnetic field.{{Refn|group = Bandai|name = card}}
*Lodestar was originally not supposed to appear in ''[[Busy Box]]'', with his role taken by [[Humungousaur (Classic)|Humungousaur]].{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/2/2e/Busy_Box_Script_Outline.pdf ''Busy Box'' Script Outline]|group = outline|name = outline}}{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/9/9f/Busy_Box_Script_First_Draft.pdf ''Busy Box'' Script First Draft]|group = script}}
*Lodestar was originally supposed to appear near the end of the dream in ''[[Night of the Living Nightmare]]'', used by Ben and [[Albedo]], instead of being used to fight [[Aggregor]].{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/d/d4/Night_of_the_Living_Nightmare_Script_First_Draft.pdf ''Night of the Living Nightmare'' Script First Draft]|group = script}}
*Lodestar's homeworld has been previously incorrectly stated to be Attracta.{{Refn|An issue of the K-Zone magazine (released before Lodestar's debut in ''[[Simple]]'') states that Lodestar's homeworld is Attracta.{{Refn|K-Zone; [[:File:Magnosapien from Attracta.png|file]]|group = mag}} However, the magazine refers to him as a Magnosapien instead of a Biotsavartian.|group = note}} and Electront.{{Refn|On October 3, 2009, an anonymous user edited Lodestar's page, claiming that Lodestar was an Elecronian from the planet Electront. The page was later edited by another anonymous on October 7, 2009, referring to Electront as a desert planet. The species and planet names would remain on the page until January 2, 2010, though they were temporarily added back to the page on March 1, 2010 by the user who originally added them to the page, before the edit was undone by [[User:Linkmadara|Linkmadara]]. ''[[Ben 10 Ultimate Alien: The Complete Guide]]'', released in September 2010, would later refer to Lodestar as an Elecronian from the desert planet Electront.{{Refn|group = guide|name = guide}} The origin of these names remains unknown.|group = note}}

